### ReturnRight customer API — local test requests
### Run from IntelliJ (HTTP Client) or VS Code (REST Client extension).
### Needs the backend running with the dev profile so the demo orders exist (see README.md).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### ─── 1. Order lookup ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1a. Mixed basket: 2 returnable, 1 window expired, 1 non-returnable
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/orders/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderNumber": "RR-10482", "email": "aditi.sharma@example.com"}

### 1b. Case and spaces are ignored
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/orders/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderNumber": "  rr-10482 ", "email": "Aditi.Sharma@Example.com"}

### 1c. Earlier returns: shoes 1 of 2 left, lamp already returned, speaker returnable again
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/orders/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderNumber": "RR-10655", "email": "vikram.singh@example.com"}

### 1d. Not delivered yet
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/orders/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderNumber": "RR-10577", "email": "rahul.verma@example.com"}

### 1e. Every window closed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/orders/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderNumber": "RR-10388", "email": "arjun.mehta@example.com"}

### 1f. Wrong email → 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/orders/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderNumber": "RR-10482", "email": "someone.else@example.com"}

### 1g. Invalid input → 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/orders/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderNumber": "", "email": "not-an-email"}

### ─── 2. Item selection ───────────────────────────────────────────

### 2a. Valid: 2 of 3 T-shirts + 1 sunscreen
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/orders/selection/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "RR-10601",
  "email": "priya.nair@example.com",
  "items": [
    {"itemId": "33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000001", "quantity": 2},
    {"itemId": "33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000002", "quantity": 1}
  ]
}

### 2b. 422: 2 shoes but only 1 left, lamp already returned, item from another order
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/orders/selection/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "RR-10655",
  "email": "vikram.singh@example.com",
  "items": [
    {"itemId": "44444444-0000-0000-0000-000000000001", "quantity": 2},
    {"itemId": "44444444-0000-0000-0000-000000000002", "quantity": 1},
    {"itemId": "33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000004", "quantity": 1}
  ]
}

### 2c. 400: empty selection
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/orders/selection/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderNumber": "RR-10601", "email": "priya.nair@example.com", "items": []}

### ─── 3. Submit return (multipart) ────────────────────────────────
### Photos: the file path is relative to this .http file. sample-photo.jpg sits next to it.

### 3a. Approved with label ready: 1 T-shirt, damaged, with a photo
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/returns
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ReturnRightBoundary

--ReturnRightBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="return"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "RR-10601",
  "email": "priya.nair@example.com",
  "items": [
    {"itemId": "33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000001", "quantity": 1,
     "reason": "DAMAGED_ON_ARRIVAL", "comment": "Hole near the collar."}
  ],
  "refundMethod": "ORIGINAL_PAYMENT",
  "detailsConfirmed": true
}
--ReturnRightBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photos.33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"; filename="sample-photo.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample-photo.jpg
--ReturnRightBoundary--

### 3b. Flagged customer (4th return in 30 days) → status REQUESTED, labelReady false
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/returns
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ReturnRightBoundary

--ReturnRightBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="return"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "RR-10702",
  "email": "meera.iyer@example.com",
  "items": [
    {"itemId": "55555555-0000-0000-0000-000000000004", "quantity": 1, "reason": "TOO_BIG"}
  ],
  "refundMethod": "STORE_CREDIT",
  "detailsConfirmed": true
}
--ReturnRightBoundary--

### 3c. 422 INVALID_PHOTOS: "Not as described" needs at least one photo
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/returns
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ReturnRightBoundary

--ReturnRightBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="return"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "RR-10601",
  "email": "priya.nair@example.com",
  "items": [
    {"itemId": "33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000002", "quantity": 1,
     "reason": "NOT_AS_DESCRIBED"}
  ],
  "refundMethod": "STORE_CREDIT",
  "detailsConfirmed": true
}
--ReturnRightBoundary--

### 3d. 400 VALIDATION_FAILED: checkbox not ticked
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/returns
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ReturnRightBoundary

--ReturnRightBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="return"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "RR-10601",
  "email": "priya.nair@example.com",
  "items": [
    {"itemId": "33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000002", "quantity": 1, "reason": "TOO_BIG"}
  ],
  "refundMethod": "STORE_CREDIT",
  "detailsConfirmed": false
}
--ReturnRightBoundary--

### ─── 4. Track a return ───────────────────────────────────────────

### 4a. Refunded at 50% after grade C ("Why ₹949.50 and not ₹1,899?")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/returns/track
Content-Type: application/json

{"rmaNumber": "RMA-DEMO-00007", "email": "neha.gupta@example.com"}

### 4b. Rejected after inspection
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/returns/track
Content-Type: application/json

{"rmaNumber": "RMA-DEMO-00008", "email": "sanjay.rao@example.com"}

### 4c. In transit, with the label
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/returns/track
Content-Type: application/json

{"rmaNumber": "RMA-DEMO-00011", "email": "farah.khan@example.com"}

### 4d. Wrong email → 404 RETURN_NOT_FOUND
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customer/returns/track
Content-Type: application/json

{"rmaNumber": "RMA-DEMO-00007", "email": "someone@example.com"}

### ─── 5. Staff sign-in (run these first; the token is saved for later requests) ─

### 5a. Warehouse agent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "riya.warehouse@returnright.example", "password": "Password@123"}

> {% client.global.set("agentToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 5b. Finance reviewer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "kavya.finance@returnright.example", "password": "Password@123"}

> {% client.global.set("financeToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 5c. Operations manager
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "manoj.ops@returnright.example", "password": "Password@123"}

> {% client.global.set("opsToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 5d. Wrong password → 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "riya.warehouse@returnright.example", "password": "wrong"}

### 5e. Who am I
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{agentToken}}

### ─── 6. Warehouse ────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 6a. Queue of received parcels
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/warehouse/returns/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{agentToken}}

### 6b. Find return (scan)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/warehouse/returns/RMA-DEMO-00006
Authorization: Bearer {{agentToken}}

### 6c. Scan in the in-transit parcel
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/warehouse/returns/RMA-DEMO-00011/receive
Authorization: Bearer {{agentToken}}

### 6d. Inspect: sweater grade C, 1 of 2 wallets accepted (partial accept) → paid at once
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/warehouse/returns/RMA-DEMO-00006/inspection
Authorization: Bearer {{agentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    {"returnItemId": "77777777-bbbb-0000-0000-000000000001", "grade": "C", "acceptedQuantity": 1},
    {"returnItemId": "77777777-bbbb-0000-0000-000000000002", "grade": "A", "acceptedQuantity": 1,
     "rejectionReason": "MISSING_PARTS_OR_TAGS", "note": "One wallet without tags"}
  ]
}

### 6e. Reject (after 6c)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/warehouse/returns/RMA-DEMO-00011/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{agentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "NOT_AS_DESCRIBED", "note": "Vase is intact, no chip found"}

### 6f. Today's counter
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/warehouse/inspections/today
Authorization: Bearer {{agentToken}}

### 6g. Finance token on a warehouse endpoint → 403 FORBIDDEN
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/warehouse/returns/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{financeToken}}

### ─── 7. Finance ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 7a. Refunds waiting for approval
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/finance/returns/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{financeToken}}

### 7b. Approve the laptop refund → REFUNDED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/finance/returns/RMA-DEMO-00009/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{financeToken}}

### ─── 8. Operations ───────────────────────────────────────────────

### 8a. Flagged returns
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/operations/returns/flagged
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}

### 8b. Approve Meera's flagged return → label ready
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/operations/returns/RMA-DEMO-00010/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}

### 8c. Or decline it (instead of 8b)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/operations/returns/RMA-DEMO-00010/decline
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"note": "Repeated returns of worn items"}
